Policy Internship
DeHavilland EU
Brussels, Belgium
€ 1,200 per month
We are looking for motivated Policy Interns to join our office in Brussels for 6 months. In this role you will support the work of the policy team with the daily monitoring, analysis and provision of insight on key regulatory and policy issues across sectors.
If you are interested in European policies and eager to lead a career in the Brussels bubble. We can offer a policy role that will boost your capabilities, your profile and your prospects.
Job responsibilities
Monitoring EU policy developments;
Contributing to updating our policy platform;
Creating concise summaries of European Parliament and Council meetings;
Supporting the publication of information on the DeHavilland platform and the curation of newsletters;
Summarising key policy developments in the interest of clients;
Supporting senior colleagues as required, depending on the policy cycles;
Participating actively in team meetings, ensuring effective communication and collaboration.
The ideal candidate would meet the following criteria
Have a relevant degree related to European policies, economics, law, social sciences or other relevant area;
Have prior experience monitoring EU policy developments;
Demonstrate interest in one or more policy fields;
Demonstrate a strong knowledge of the functioning of the European Union;
Have strong writing skills in English (fluent);
Be curious and eager to learn more about policies;
Have a solid attention to detail;
Be able to keep up in a fast-paced environment;
Have interpersonal skills and can integrate within a multicultural team.
Apply Now
Don't forget to mention EuroBrussels when applying.
