The candidate will be required to demonstrate that he/she has:
a minimum of fifteen (15) years of relevant professional experience, acquired after the award of the academic qualification required as a condition of eligibility;
substantial professional experience in multinational working environments, including in a managerial position, with a proven track record in leading multinational and multidisciplinary teams at senior and/or middle-management level and fostering cooperation across diverse national and organisational contexts;
very good knowledge of and substantial professional experience in defence planning and capability development, including the identification and prioritisation of capability needs and the development of collaborative opportunities;
broad knowledge of capability development across multiple operational domains and/or strategic enabling areas, with a good understanding of cross-domain dependencies and requirements;
good knowledge of the European institutional and defence cooperation framework, including relevant EU defence policies, programmes and initiatives and the main EU capability-development planning processes;
sound knowledge of collaborative capability development and armaments cooperation in a European or multinational context, including the harmonisation of requirements and the development of cooperative projects or programmes;
proven experience in translating defence priorities, capability requirements or planning outcomes into strategic recommendations, collaborative initiatives or capability-development activities;

