Contribute to the development and implementation of the SFC’s policy and advocacy strategy;
Develop and maintain strong relationships with EU officials, policymakers, industry associations and other relevant stakeholders, strengthening cooperation with existing partners and identifying opportunities for new alliances;
Represent the SFC and its members in meetings with policymakers, regulators, industry stakeholders and other external partners;
Support the Managing Director on policy, advocacy and other strategic matters as required and deputise for the Managing Director when necessary.
Qualifications and Experience
At least 10 years of relevant professional experience in EU-level public policy, regulatory affairs or governmental affairs within the financial services sector;
Strong knowledge and experience of asset management regulation is highly desirable;
Proven experience in regulatory and policy positioning and advocacy at European and/or international level;
In-depth understanding of the political and regulatory challenges facing the financial sector, ideally including the relationship between the EU and third-country financial centres;
Strong understanding of EU institutions, decision-making processes and legislative procedures;
A strong track record in senior stakeholder management and engagement;
Experience in leading, managing or coordinating a team is highly desirable.
Skills and Competencies
Strong analytical skills and the ability to quickly understand and assess complex policy and regulatory issues;
Strong organisational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively;
Strong leadership and coordination skills, combined with a collaborative working style;
A proactive, pragmatic and solution-oriented mindset, with the ability to work effectively in a dynamic environment;
A high degree of autonomy, flexibility and sound judgement;
Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English. Fluency in German and/or French is an asset;
Excellent interpersonal skills and the ability to build strong relationships with members and external stakeholders;
Professional proficiency in Microsoft Outlook, Word and PowerPoint.
What We Offer
A senior role with significant responsibility within a small and highly engaged team;
A dynamic and international working environment at the heart of European financial policymaking;
The opportunity to work across a wide range of policy issues and engage with senior stakeholders from the financial sector and EU institutions;
A permanent, full-time position with a competitive salary package and additional benefits;
A modern workplace in the European quarter in Brussels, with the possibility of part-time home office.
